President Trump has made it clear: criminal illegal aliens are NOT welcome in the United States of America

WASHINGTON –– U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) today announced the arrest of more criminal illegal aliens from across the country, convicted of murder, possession of obscene matter depicting a minor engaged in sexual conduct, and kidnapping of an adult to sexually assault.

> The heroic men and women of ICE never take a day off, even over the weekend. Thanks to our law enforcement, we have fewer murderers, child predators, and gang members on our streets,

said Deputy Assistant Secretary Lauren Bis.

> Under President Trump, if you come to our country illegally and break our laws, we will find you and arrest you. The safety of the American people comes FIRST.

Arrests over the weekend include:

Image

Romualdo Ruiz-Erazo, a criminal illegal alien from Honduras, convicted of second-degree murder in Durham County, North Carolina.

Image

